{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And not with a mighty hand</b> — as long as I do not make known to him My mighty hand, he will not let you go. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 3:19): And the correct interpretation in my eyes is, <b>he will not let you go</b> to depart by speech, <b>and not with a mighty hand</b> — until I send <b>My hand against all My wonders that I will do in his midst</b>, with a mighty hand and with an outstretched arm and with great terror and with signs and with portents, <b>and after that he will send you away</b>, for all of them came upon him before he let them go:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:16:37.353165104Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}